<DocsLayout title="Limitations" description="Understand the current single-host boundaries before using MyPaaS.">
<section><p class="overline">Scope</p><h2>Single host by design</h2><p>MyPaaS runs its control plane and project workloads on one Linux host. The VM remains the capacity and availability boundary.</p></section>
<section><h2>Current boundaries</h2><ul><li>No public signup, hosted plans, or billing.</li><li>No Kubernetes or multi-node scheduling.</li><li>No multi-region high availability or automatic horizontal scaling.</li><li>Registry deployment currently targets public OCI images.</li><li>Static recovery uses redeploy or roll-forward instead of container rollback.</li></ul></section>
<section><h2>Operator responsibility</h2><p>Host capacity, provider availability, backup verification, and recovery material remain the operator's responsibility.</p></section>
</DocsLayout>
